<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingston, Jamaica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kingston is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, on a deep natural harbour on the south-east coast. It was founded in 1692 for survivors of the earthquake that destroyed nearby Port Royal and grew into the island's chief port and commercial centre. It replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-town">Spanish Town</a> as the capital in 1872, and it was largely rebuilt after an earthquake and fire in 1907.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingston-jamaica.jpg" alt="Kingston, Jamaica" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Blofeld of SPECTRE at English Wikipedia. (Original text: W. Harris) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortofKingston.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
